// Generated by scripts/build-help-kb.py — edit scripts/help-current.md or the help pages, then rerun.
export const HELP_KB = "# CURRENT FACTS ABOUT QUOTABLE (always right; use these first)\n\n## What Quotable is\nQuotable is quoting, invoicing and scheduling software for UK tradespeople, made by Quotable Ltd. Website: quotable.uk. Support email: support@quotable-it.co.uk.\n\n## Making a quote\nGo to Quotes, then Create Quote. Describe the job in your own words, typed or by tapping the microphone to speak. Quotable lists the materials and quantities, prices each one, and works out labour from your rate. You can edit any line before saving or sending.\nFor accurate quotes include: measurements (room sizes in metres, lengths, number of items), the job location or postcode area, what's there now and what's being replaced, the finish or product quality wanted, and access issues (stairs, parking, height). Example: \"Re-skim the bedroom walls, about 3 m by 3 m, walls sound\" is better than \"plaster a room\".\nSet your hourly rate and day rate in Account, under your trade details. Labour on quotes uses your rate.\nAnything Quotable couldn't price is marked so you can check it. Always check quantities and prices before sending: the AI's suggestions are a starting point and you're responsible for the quote you send.\nThere is a fair-use limit of 60 AI quotes per account per day.\n\n## Where prices come from\nMaterial prices are read from UK merchants' product pages, mainly Toolstation, Wickes and Travis Perkins, and each priced line shows its source. Your own Inventory prices are always used first when an item matches. Prices are refreshed regularly; trade-account, in-store or delivery prices can differ. Items marked as an estimate couldn't be matched to a real product. Quotable isn't connected with or endorsed by any merchant.\nInventory: add items you buy regularly with your own prices (Inventory in the sidebar, Add Item), or save a material from a quote.\n\n## Sending a quote and getting it accepted\nOpen a quote and use Send. You can send a link by WhatsApp, email, or copy the link to send another way. The customer opens it on their phone without an account, and can accept with a tap. You can see when it's been opened and accepted.\nTo let customers pay a deposit or invoice from the link, add a card payment link (for example your own Stripe, SumUp or PayPal link) and your bank details in Account, under Brand Details.\nTo stop a link working, open the quote's Send window and choose Stop sharing this link. Sending again makes a new link.\n\n## Invoices\nIn Invoices, use Convert to Invoice on an accepted quote. Mark an invoice as paid when the money arrives. Overdue invoices are highlighted. Invoices can be sent by link the same way as quotes. Export invoices for Xero, QuickBooks or FreeAgent from the export menu on the Invoices page.\n\n## VAT and tax\nIf you're VAT-registered, set your VAT rate (20% standard in the UK) in Settings; it's added to quotes and invoices. Tax & Reports shows revenue, tax collected and outstanding invoices, and exports reports for your accountant. Quotable doesn't give tax advice.\n\n## Scheduling\nScheduling shows jobs on a calendar. Add an accepted quote to a date and set how long it takes; drag to move on a computer. Colours show quote, scheduled, completed, overdue and paid.\n\n## Clients\nClients stores customer names, addresses and contact details so you can reuse them on quotes and invoices.\n\n## PDF templates and branding\nAdd your logo, business name, address and colours in Account, under Brand Details. PDF templates (in the sidebar) let you choose and design how quotes and invoices look.\n\n## The sample account\n\"Look around with sample data\" opens a demo account with example quotes and invoices. Nothing you change there is saved.\n\n## Using Quotable on your phone\nAdd it to your home screen to use it like an app: on iPhone in Safari tap Share then Add to Home Screen; on Android in Chrome tap the menu then Install app. Full steps at quotable.uk/app.\n\n## Plans and billing\n\u00a314.99 a month or \u00a3159.99 a year, with the first month free for new customers. Cancel any time in the app: Account, then Cancel subscription (two taps). You keep access until the end of the period you've paid for. \"Change plan, card or invoices\" in Account opens the billing portal to switch monthly/yearly, update your card or download invoices. Promo codes can be entered at checkout or shared as links like quotable.uk/?code=CODE.\n\n## Account and data\nSign in with email and password or with Google. Reset a forgotten password from the sign-in page. To close your account and delete your data, email support. Data is stored securely; see the privacy policy at quotable.uk/privacy. Terms are at quotable.uk/terms.\n\n## Pricing guides for trades\nFree guides on pricing common jobs (materials, labour hours, worked examples) are at quotable.uk/guides, day rates by trade and region at quotable.uk/day-rates, and printable quote templates at quotable.uk/quote-templates.\n\n\n# OLDER HELP ARTICLES (where these disagree with CURRENT FACTS above, the current facts are right)\n\n## Article: /help/accurate-quotes\nGetting the Most Accurate Quote How do I break down labour costs properly? Labour costs should reflect the actual time and number of workers needed. Be specific about tasks\u2014for example, \"Demolition 2 workers, 4 hours \" is clearer than just \"Labour.\" Include your hourly rate and multiply by hours worked. Don't forget to account for setup and cleanup time. What should I include in materials? List every material needed with accurate quantities and unit prices. Include consumables like screws, adhesive, and paint. Add a small buffer 5-10% for waste or mistakes. If you're uncertain about prices, check recent invoices or supplier websites to get current rates. Should I include overheads in my quotes? Yes. Overheads like travel, fuel, equipment rental, permits, and disposal fees should be itemized separately. This transparency shows clients exactly what they're paying for and helps justify your total price. Don't hide these costs\u2014clients appreciate clarity. How do I avoid underquoting a job? Always visit the job site before quoting. Take measurements, photos, and notes. Ask questions about the client's expectations. Include contingency time 10-15% for unexpected issues. Review similar past jobs to check if your estimates are realistic. If in doubt, slightly overestimate\u2014it's easier to come in under budget than over. What if my quote total seems too high or too low? If it seems too high, double-check your quantities and rates. Compare with industry standards. If it's too low, you may have missed materials, underestimated time, or forgotten overheads. Use Quotable's AI summary to review what's included\u2014it can catch missing items or calculation errors. Can I save quote templates for repeat jobs? Yes, use the Templates section in Settings to save frequently used items and rates. This speeds up quoting and ensures consistency across similar jobs. You can adjust quantities and descriptions for each new quote while keeping your pricing accurate. How do I use the Manual Edit feature to adjust my quote? After generating a quote, click the edit icon pencil in the quote breakdown. This opens a dialog where you can manually adjust any line item\u2014change quantities, costs, add or remove items from materials, labour, or overheads. Changes update the total in real-time. Click \"Revert\" to undo changes, or \"Save Changes\" to apply them. This is perfect for fine-tuning quotes based on supplier pricing or client negotiations. What is the AI Adjuster and how does it work? The AI Adjuster lightning bolt icon lets you adjust your quote using natural language. Instead of manually editing each item, simply describe what you want\u2014for example, \"Reduce labour by 10%\", \"Add 15% contingency buffer\", or \"Increase material costs by 5% due to supplier changes\". The AI will intelligently apply these adjustments across your quote. This is ideal for quick percentage changes, adding buffers, or making proportional adjustments to multiple line items at once. ; ; export default AccurateQuotes;\n\n## Article: /help/clients\nClient Management  How do I add a new client? Go to Clients in the sidebar and click \"Add Client\". Enter the company name required , contact name, email, phone, address, and any notes. You can also add clients directly when creating quotes or invoices. How do I view a client's job history? Click on any client card to open their details drawer. You'll see all quotes and invoices associated with that client, along with total revenue and job counts. Click on any quote or invoice to view its details. Can I import clients from existing quotes? Yes! On the Clients page, look for the \"Import from Quotes/Invoices\" button shows a badge with the count . Click it to see client names from your quotes that aren't saved yet. Click \"+\" to add them as contacts. How do I use saved clients in new quotes? When creating a quote, start typing the client name and you'll see matching saved clients. Select one to auto-fill their details address, email, phone . You can also click the dropdown to browse all clients. How do I edit or delete a client? Click on the client card, then use the Edit or Delete buttons in the details drawer. Note: deleting a client doesn't delete their associated quotes or invoices - those remain in your records. What does the revenue stat show? The revenue shown on each client card is the total from all paid invoices for that client. It helps you identify your most valuable customers and track business relationships over time. ; ; export default ClientsHelp;\n\n## Article: /help/common-issues\nCommon Issues My quote total doesn't match what I expected Check that tax is being applied correctly in Settings. Verify that labour, materials, and overheads are calculated properly. Make sure you haven't accidentally included the same item twice. Use the AI summary to review all included items and spot any errors. I can't edit or delete a saved quote Make sure you're logged in and not in demo mode. Only quotes you created can be edited or deleted. If the quote has been converted to an invoice, you may need to edit the invoice instead. Try refreshing the page if buttons aren't responding. PDF exports aren't working or look wrong Ensure your brand information is filled out in Settings\u2014especially your business name and logo. Check that your browser allows pop-ups from Quotable. Try a different PDF template in Settings. If the layout looks broken, make sure all required fields client name, job description, items are completed. My data disappeared after logging out If you were in demo mode, your data won't save\u2014that's by design. Create an account to save your quotes, invoices, and schedules permanently. If you had an account and data is missing, make sure you're logged into the correct email address. The site is slow or not loading properly Clear your browser cache and cookies, then refresh. Check your internet connection. Try using a different browser or device. If the issue persists, it may be a temporary server problem\u2014wait a few minutes and try again. I'm not receiving email notifications Check your spam/junk folder. Verify that email notifications are enabled in Settings. Make sure the email address on your account is correct. Add Quotable to your email contacts or safe senders list to prevent future emails from being blocked. ; ; export default CommonIssues;\n\n## Article: /help/contact\nContact Support Can't find what you're looking for? Our support team is here to help. Choose the best way to reach us below. Email Support For general inquiries, billing questions, or technical issues that aren't urgent. support@quotable-it.co.uk Response time: Within 24-48 hours Live Chat For urgent issues or if you need immediate assistance with the app. Available Monday - Friday, 9am - 5pm GMT Coming Soon Before You Contact Us \u2022 Check if your question is answered in the Help sections above \u2022 Try basic troubleshooting steps like clearing your cache or refreshing the page \u2022 Include details like browser type, device, and screenshots when reporting issues \u2022 Provide your account email so we can look up your account details ; ; export default Contact;\n\n## Article: /help/demo-mode\nDemo Mode What is demo mode? Demo mode lets you explore Quotable without creating an account. You'll see sample quotes, invoices, and schedules that demonstrate how the system works. It's a fully functional preview so you can test features before signing up. Why can't I save data in demo mode? Demo mode is read-only. Any changes you make won't be saved when you close the tab or refresh the page. This is intentional\u2014it keeps the demo clean for everyone. To save your own quotes, invoices, and schedules, you need to subscribe to Quotable Pro. Can I create a quote in demo mode? Yes, you can create one temporary quote to test the quote builder. However, it won't be saved and you can't export it as a PDF. Once you refresh or leave the page, it will disappear. For full functionality, sign up for an account. How do I switch from demo mode to a real account? Click \"Get Started\" or \"Create Account\" to sign up. Once logged in, you'll have full access to save quotes, create invoices, schedule jobs, and export PDFs. Your account data is completely separate from demo data and persists across sessions. Is demo mode the same on mobile and desktop? Yes, demo mode works the same on all devices. You'll see the same sample data and features, adapted for mobile or desktop layout. The only difference is the interface\u2014mobile uses a collapsible menu and optimised touch controls. Can I access demo mode after creating an account? Once you're logged in, you'll see your real data instead of demo data. You can log out to re-enter demo mode, but it's recommended to stay logged in to access all features and keep your work saved. ; ; export default DemoMode;\n\n## Article: /help/inventory-pricing\nInventory & Pricing  What is the inventory system? The inventory lets you store commonly-used parts with your actual prices. When generating quotes, the AI checks your inventory first and uses your prices for matching items. This ensures consistent, accurate pricing. How do I add items to inventory? Go to Inventory in the sidebar and click \"Add Item\". Enter the item name, unit each, metre, pack, etc. , unit price, and optionally a category and description. You can also save items directly from generated quotes using the \"Save\" button next to each material. Where do the material prices come from? Prices are sourced from UK merchants including Toolstation, Screwfix, City Plumbing, and trade suppliers. Prices are refreshed nightly, and anything we could not match to a real product is marked as an estimate. Look for the source badge on each item e.g., \"Toolstation\", \"Inventory\", \"Estimated\" to see where the price originated. What do the confidence badges mean? Green \u226585% = Verified price from a supplier. Yellow 70-84% = Estimated based on similar products. Red <70% = Market average, less reliable. Inventory items always show 100% confidence since they're your actual prices. How do preferred suppliers work? In Account Settings, you can select preferred suppliers based on your trade. The quote generator will prioritise prices from your preferred suppliers when available. This helps ensure quotes reflect where you actually buy materials. Why is a price showing as \"Estimated\"? If we can't find an exact match in our database or your inventory, we estimate the price based on similar products and market data. These items are included to ensure your quote is complete. Consider adding accurate prices to your inventory for frequently-used items. ; ; export default InventoryPricingHelp;\n\n## Article: /help/quote-templates\nQuote Templates  What are quote templates? Quote templates let you save common job configurations materials, labour, overheads for reuse. Instead of generating from scratch every time, you can load a template and just fill in the client details. Perfect for repeat jobs. How do I save a quote as a template? After generating or editing a quote, click \"Save as Template\". Give it a name e.g., \"Standard Rewire - 3 Bed House\" and the job details, materials, labour, and overheads will be saved. Client-specific info like name and address are not included. How do I use a saved template? On the Quotes page, look for the Templates tab. Browse your saved templates and click \"Use Template\" to pre-fill a new quote form. Add the client details and make any adjustments needed, then save as a new quote. Can I edit or delete templates? Yes, in the Templates tab you can edit any template to update materials, labour, or overheads. You can also delete templates you no longer need. Changes to templates don't affect quotes already created from them. Do template prices update automatically? No, templates save the prices at the time they were created. When you use a template, you may want to regenerate prices using the AI or update them manually to reflect current market rates. What's the difference between templates and inventory? Inventory stores individual items with prices e.g., \"15mm copper pipe - \u00a32.50/m\" . Templates store complete job configurations with all materials, labour, and overheads together e.g., \"Full bathroom refit\" . Use both together for maximum efficiency. ; ; export default QuoteTemplatesHelp;\n\n## Article: /help/scheduling\nScheduling & Calendar How do I add a job to the calendar? On desktop, drag an unscheduled quote from the left panel onto a date in the calendar. On mobile, tap the quote, select a start date, and set the duration. The job will appear on the calendar as a colored block spanning the days you specified. What do the different colors mean? Blue = Quote not yet confirmed , Yellow = Scheduled confirmed job , Green = Completed, Red = Overdue, Teal = Paid. These colors help you quickly see the status of each job at a glance. You can check the color legend on the scheduling page for reference. How do I change a job's duration or start date? Click or tap the job on the calendar to open its details. You can edit the start date, end date, or duration. On desktop, you can also drag the job to a new date or resize it by dragging the edges. Changes save automatically. What are the shaded areas on the calendar? Shaded areas indicate payment windows\u2014the 30-day period after an invoice is sent when payment is expected. The shading gets more intense as the due date approaches. This helps you track outstanding invoices and follow up on overdue payments. Can I see jobs in different views day, week, month ? Yes. Use the view switcher at the top of the scheduling page to toggle between Day, Week, and Month views. Each view shows different levels of detail\u2014Month is great for planning ahead, Week for current jobs, and Day for detailed time slots. How do I mark a job as completed or paid? Click the job on the calendar to open details, then use the \"Mark Completed\" or \"Mark Paid\" buttons. You can also update the status from the Invoices page. Once marked, the job's color will change to reflect its new status green for completed, teal for paid . Why can't I schedule a quote? Make sure the quote has been saved and isn't in draft mode. Check that you're logged in and not in demo mode. If the quote has already been scheduled, it won't appear in the unscheduled list\u2014look for it on the calendar instead. ; ; export default Scheduling;\n\n## Article: /help/tax-pricing\nTax & Pricing How is tax calculated on quotes and invoices? Tax is calculated based on the rate you set in Settings e.g., 20% for UK VAT . It's applied to the subtotal labour + materials + overheads to give your grand total. The tax rate is shown clearly on all quotes and invoices. Make sure to set the correct rate for your region. Can I change the tax rate for specific jobs? Currently, the tax rate is set globally in Settings and applies to all quotes and invoices. If you need to charge a different rate for a specific client or job type, you'll need to adjust it manually in Settings before creating that quote, then change it back afterward. Where can I see my total tax collected? Go to the Tax & Reports page to see a summary of total tax collected, revenue, and outstanding invoices. You can filter by date range and export reports as PDFs for your accountant or tax filing. This helps you stay on top of your tax obligations throughout the year. Why is my total different from what I quoted the client? Check if you've accidentally changed quantities, rates, or the tax rate since creating the quote. Verify that all materials, labour, and overheads are included correctly. If you edited the quote after sending it, make sure you sent the updated version to the client. Do I need to register for VAT or sales tax? This depends on your country and annual revenue. In the UK, you must register for VAT if your taxable turnover exceeds \u00a385,000 per year. In the US, sales tax rules vary by state. Consult a local accountant or tax advisor to understand your specific obligations. How do I avoid double-charging for labour or materials? When creating a quote, separate labour and materials into distinct line items. Don't include material costs in your labour hourly rate. List each material individually with its own price. Review the AI-generated summary to ensure nothing is listed twice. This keeps pricing transparent and accurate. ; ; export default TaxPricing;\n\n## Article: /help/templates\nTemplates & Items What are the different PDF templates? Quotable offers three PDF templates: Minimalist clean and simple , Modern bold and colorful , and Classic traditional and professional . You can preview each template in Settings before choosing one. The template you select will be used for all quotes and invoices you export. How do I customize my PDF template? Go to Settings and update your brand information\u2014company name, logo, address, phone, email, and VAT number. This info appears on all PDFs. You can also choose which template style to use. Currently, the layout and colors of each template are fixed, but your branding is fully customizable. Can I save frequently used items or rates? Yes, use the Templates section in Settings to save common items like materials, equipment, or standard labour rates. When creating a new quote, you can quickly add these saved items instead of retyping them each time. This speeds up quoting and ensures consistency. Why can't I edit a locked template? Some templates are locked to preserve standard formatting. If you need more customization, try duplicating the template and editing the copy. Alternatively, create a new custom template from scratch. Locked templates ensure consistency and prevent accidental changes to default styles. How do I add my logo to quotes and invoices? Go to Settings \u2192 Brand Information and upload your logo. It will appear on all PDF exports automatically. Use a high-quality image PNG or JPG with a transparent background for best results. The logo is positioned in the header section of your PDFs. Can I have different templates for quotes vs invoices? Currently, the same template applies to both quotes and invoices. However, the document type Quote or Invoice is clearly labeled in the header, and invoice-specific fields like due date and payment status are automatically included. Future updates may allow separate template selection. ; ; export default Templates;\n\n## Article: /help/troubleshooting\nTroubleshooting The app isn't loading or shows a blank screen Clear your browser cache and cookies, then refresh the page. Try opening Quotable in a private/incognito window. If that works, the issue is with cached data. Check your internet connection and make sure JavaScript is enabled in your browser settings. Buttons or links aren't responding when I click them Refresh the page and try again. Disable browser extensions especially ad blockers to see if they're interfering. Try a different browser. If the issue persists on mobile, restart your device and ensure you're using the latest version of your browser. My data isn't syncing across devices Make sure you're logged into the same account on all devices. Check your internet connection\u2014data syncs require a stable connection. If you made changes on one device, wait a few seconds and refresh the other device. Log out and back in if the issue continues. I'm getting error messages when creating quotes or invoices Check that all required fields are filled out\u2014client name, job description, and at least one item. Make sure numbers are formatted correctly no letters in quantity or price fields . If you're copying and pasting, remove any extra characters or formatting. Try creating a simpler version first to isolate the problem. The site looks broken or text is overlapping This is usually a browser caching issue. Clear your cache and hard refresh Ctrl+Shift+R on Windows, Cmd+Shift+R on Mac . If you're on mobile, try rotating your device or zooming in/out. Update your browser to the latest version. I forgot my password and can't log in Click \"Forgot Password\" on the login page and follow the email instructions to reset it. Check your spam folder if you don't receive the email. If you signed up with Google, use \"Continue with Google\" instead of entering a password. If you can't remember your email, contact support. The PDF I downloaded is corrupted or won't open Try downloading the PDF again\u2014it may have been interrupted. Check that your PDF viewer is up to date Adobe Reader, browser PDF viewer, etc. . Try opening it in a different program. If the problem persists, generate the PDF again from the quote or invoice page. ; ; export default Troubleshooting;";
